;; I, Behind the Wall. Up from J by the rough face (column 1). The crack
;; in the west wall looks into the chamber. The air shaft from M tops out
;; under the roof (row 1) and steps west onto the high ledge (17-20, row 2),
;; six rows above the floor and out of a jump's reach; drop from it through
;; the gap (16) to the floor.
(room
  region: underhum
  at: (8 5)
  title: "Behind the Wall"
  intent: "a narrow passage behind the chamber's east wall, where a crack shows the hollow beyond: a breath"
  bed: (hum 0.7 air 0.4 water 0)
  light: 0.2
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "################      ^^#"
   "################      ^^#"
   "################ #####^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#                    #^^#"
   "#%  ##################^^#"
   "#%  ##################^^#")
  things: ((crack at: (1 6)))
  decor: none)
